<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Give operator status to a user in the current channel. This is a shorthand for"
  )} <code>{dgettext("help_commands", "/mode +o nickname")}</code>.
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_question}>{dgettext("help_commands", "When to Use It")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Give operator status to someone you trust to help run the channel. Operators can kick and ban users, change the topic when it is locked, pin messages and set channel modes."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_code}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Syntax")}</.help_h4>
<pre>{dgettext("help_commands", "/op <nickname>")}</pre>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tag}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Parameters")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <code>nickname</code> {dgettext("help_commands", "— The user to promote to operator.")}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_control}>{dgettext("help_commands", "How It Works")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "The command acts on the channel you are viewing. A member holds one channel role at a time, so the new operator role replaces any voice or half-operator status the user had. Everyone in the channel sees a mode change line, and the user moves to the Operator group in the nick list."
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Status given with this command lasts until the user leaves the channel. When they join again in a registered channel, their status comes from the ChanServ access list. In an unregistered channel, they come back as a regular member."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Rules & Limits")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "Requires operator (@) or owner (~) status in the channel")}</li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "The target must be in the channel")}</li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "Half-operators cannot give operator status")}</li>
  <li>
    {dgettext("help_commands", "Only the first nickname is used. Extra words are ignored.")}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_commands",
      "You must type it in a channel window, not in a private conversation"
    )}
  </li>
</ul>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Examples")}</.help_h4>
<pre>{dgettext("help_commands", "/op Alice")}</pre>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_commands", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="cmd-deop">{dgettext("help_commands", "/deop")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="ui-context-menu">
    {dgettext("help_commands", "Context Menu")}
  </.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-voice">{dgettext("help_commands", "/voice")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-mode">{dgettext("help_commands", "/mode")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="mode-o">{dgettext("help_commands", "+o Operator")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="chanserv-access">
    {dgettext("help_commands", "ChanServ Access Lists")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="channel-permissions">
    {dgettext("help_commands", "Channel Permissions")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
